---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "August 24, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Independent Society"
  description="How Independent Society collects, uses, and protects your data."
>
  <article class="container article-wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="article-lead">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information Independent Society
        (independentsociety.space, "the Site", "we") collects when you visit
        or use the Site, and how that information is used.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Independent Society is an independently run blog. If you have any
        questions about this policy or your data, you can reach us at  
         <a href="mailto:suprun.jen@gmail.com">suprun.jen@gmail.com</a> or via
        the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect only what's needed to run the features on this Site:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account &amp; sign-in:</strong> if you sign in to comment or
          react to a post, we collect the email address you provide. Sign-in
          uses a passwordless "magic link" — we never see or store a
          password.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Comments:</strong> if you post a comment, the comment text,
          the time it was posted, and its association with your account are
          stored so the comment can be displayed on the relevant post.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reactions:</strong> likes/dislikes on posts are stored and
          linked to your account so each account can only react once per
          post.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic technical data:</strong> like most websites, our
          hosting provider automatically logs standard technical information
          (such as IP address and browser type) for security and reliability
          purposes.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not collect payment information, and we do not currently run
        any advertising or analytics tracking on the Site beyond what's
        described below.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To let you sign in and keep you signed in between visits</li>
        <li>To display your comments and reactions on posts</li>
        <li>To keep the Site secure and prevent abuse</li>
        <li>To understand, in aggregate, how the Site is found and used, so we can improve it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with third parties for their own marketing purposes.</p>

      <h2>Third-party services we use</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on a small number of third-party services to run the Site.
        Each only receives the data it needs to perform its function:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> — provides authentication (magic-link
          sign-in) and stores account, comment, and reaction data on our
          behalf. See
          <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Vercel</strong> — hosts the Site and handles standard
          technical/server logs. See
          <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Search Console</strong> — used by us to monitor how
          the Site performs in Google Search. It does not collect personal
          data from visitors; it reports aggregate search performance data to
          us. See
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use a cookie set by Supabase to keep you signed in between visits.
        This is a functional cookie required for the sign-in, commenting, and
        reactions features to work — we don't use cookies for advertising or
        cross-site tracking.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        The only data we hold about you is the email address you signed in
        with, and any comments or reactions posted under your account. You
        can ask us to see, correct, export, or delete this data at any time
        by emailing
         <a href="mailto:suprun.jen@gmail.com">suprun.jen@gmail.com</a>.
        Deleting your account will remove your stored email address; you may
        also ask us to remove specific comments.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Site is not directed at children under 16, and we do not
        knowingly collect personal data from children.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the Site changes — for example, if we
        add analytics or advertising in the future, we'll update this page
        to reflect exactly what's added and how it affects your data. We'll
        update the "Last updated" date above whenever we make changes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>